"hadiths[46]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1034,"It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira and Hazrat Zaid bin Khalid Jahni that a villager came to the service of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of Allah! I swear to you by Allah that you judge me according to the Book of Allah. And the other one who was wiser than him also said yes! You decide between us according to the Book of Allah and allow me to submit something. He said: ""Explain."" He said: My son used to work as a laborer for him. He committed adultery with his wife and I was informed that the punishment of stoning was necessary for my son. After that, I inquired from the scholars and they told me that my son's punishment is 100 lashes and one year's exile and his wife's punishment is imprisonment. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""By the One in Whose hand is my soul!"" I will judge between you according to the Book of Allah. The slave girls and the goats will be returned to you and your son will be punished with a hundred lashes and exile for a year. And oh nineteen! Go to this man's wife, and if she confesses (to adultery), stone her to death."" (Bukhari and Muslim and these words are from Muslim)."
1035,"On the authority of Hazrat Ubada bin Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Get (the rules of Sharia) from me."" Get it from me. Allah has made clear the way for women. If a virgin boy commits adultery with a virgin girl, his punishment is 100 lashes and one year exile. And if a married man commits adultery with a married woman, his punishment is one hundred lashes and stoning.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
1036,"It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah that a Muslim man came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the mosque. You turned away from him. He came to you from the other side and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have committed adultery. He then turned his face towards the Anwar until the man repeated his words four times. So (in this way) when he testified against himself four times, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him to him and asked: ""Are you mad?"" He said: No. He then said: ""Are you married?"" He said: Yes. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Take him and stone him."" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
1037,"It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that when Ma'az bin Malik (RA) came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH), he asked him: ""Perhaps you have kissed or teased or cast an evil eye."" He said: ""No, O Messenger of Allah!"" (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
1038,"On the authority of Hazrat Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said in his address: Allah, the Exalted, appointed Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as His Messenger and revealed the Book to him. In what Allah revealed to you, there was also the verse of stoning. We (ourselves) read it and memorized it and understood it (well). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned him and we also stoned him after him. I fear that after some time someone will say that we do not find any mention of stoning in the Book of Allah. In this way, those people will go astray by abandoning a duty that Allah revealed, although the punishment of stoning is established in the Book of Allah for every married man and woman when there is evidence or pregnancy or confession (of adultery and adultery). (Bukhari and Muslim)"
1039,"It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: ""When the slave girl of one of you is guilty of adultery and her adultery becomes apparent, then he should restrain her and not reprimand her."" If he commits adultery again, he should limit it and not reprimand him. If he commits adultery for the third time and his adultery is revealed, then sell him, even if it is for a rope made of hair."" (Bukhari and Muslim) and these words are from Muslim."
1040,It is narrated from Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Set limits on your slaves and concubines.”
1041,"It is narrated from Hazrat Imran bin Hussain that a woman from Jahina tribe came to the Prophet and she was pregnant by adultery. He said: O Prophet of Allah! I deserve a limit, so impose a limit on me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called her guardian and advised him: ""Be kind to her and when she gives birth, bring her to me."" So he did so. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered about her (the woman), so her clothes were tied tightly. Then he gave an order about her and she was stoned to death. Then he offered her funeral prayer, Hazrat Umar said: O Prophet of Allah! You offer her funeral prayer even though she was guilty of adultery? He said: ""He has repented in such a way that if he were to be distributed among seventy people of Madinah, he would surround them all."" Have you found someone better than him who has laid down his life for the sake of Allah?” (Narrated by Muslim)."
1042,It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) stoned a man from the tribe of Islam and stoned a Jewish man and a woman. (It was narrated by Muslim. And the incident of the stoning of a Jewish man and a woman is narrated in Sahihin on the authority of Ibn Umar.)
1043,"It was narrated from Hazrat Saeed bin Saad bin Ubadah that there used to be a small crippled man in our neighborhood. He committed adultery with one of our slave girls. Hazrat Sa'd (RA) mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), so he said: ""Put a limit on it."" Then he said: ""O Messenger of Allah! He is much weaker and weaker than that. He said: ""Take a large branch of a palm tree with a hundred branches, then strike it at the man once."" So they did so. (It was narrated by Ahmad al-Nasa’i and Ibn Majah and its chain of transmission is good, but there is a difference in its transmission and transmission.)"
1044,"It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever you find guilty of the actions of the people of Lut, kill both the perpetrator and the victim."" And whoever you find misbehaving with a cow, kill both the man and the cow."
1045,"It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed (an unmarried adulteress) and exiled her. And Hazrat Abu Bakr (RA) was also killed and exiled. And Hazrat Umar also killed and exiled. (It was narrated by Tirmidhi and its narrators are reliable, but there is a difference of opinion regarding whether it was suspended or abrogated.)"
1046,"It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed men who impersonate women and cursed women who impersonate men."
1047,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As far as there is room for protection from imposing a limit, remove the limit.” (It was narrated by Ibn Majah and its chain of transmission is weak.) And it was narrated by Tirmidhi and Al-Hakim on the authority of Hazrat Aisha, Radiyallahu Anhu, with these words: “Remove the limits from the Muslims as far as you can.” (This is also weak.) What has been narrated on the authority of Radiyallahu Anhu? And that is Hazrat Ali's own saying, whose words are: Remove the limits due to doubts."
1048,"On the authority of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Beware of those dirty deeds which Allah has forbidden."" And whoever suffers from them, he should remain hidden in the veil placed by Allah and he should repent to the Lord of Allah (in secret), because whoever reveals his case to us, we will enforce the command of Allah and leave him.”"
1049,"It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (RA) that when my acquittal was revealed in the Holy Qur'an, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) stood on the pulpit and mentioned it and recited the Qur'an. When he came down from the pulpit, he decided on two men and one woman and they were restricted. (Narrated by Ahmad and Al-Charu and referred to by Bukhari.)"
1050,"It is narrated from Hazrat Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the first incident of blasphemy in Islam was by Sharik bin Sahma. He was accused by Hilal bin Umayyah of adultery with his wife. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: ""Bring evidence, otherwise you will be punished."" (Then) the narrator narrated the entire hadith. (This hadith has been narrated by Abu Al-Ala and its narrator is Thaqa. And in Bukhari, a similar hadith has been narrated on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him.)"
1051,"On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi'ah, I have found the covenant of Hazrat Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and those after them. I did not see them punishing slaves with more than forty lashes. (Narrated by Malik and narrated by Al-Thawri in his Jama`ah.)"
1052,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever slanders his slave (or concubine), he will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, unless it is as he has said, that is, (that slander is true.”) (Bukhari and Muslim)."
1053,"Narrated by Hazrat Aisha, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""A thief's hand should be cut off for stealing a quarter of a dinar or more."" (Bukhari and Muslim - these words are from Muslim). And Bukhari's words are: ""A thief's hand will be cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more."""
1054,It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off his hand while stealing a shield worth three dirhams. (Bukhari and Muslim)
1055,"It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""May the curse of Allah be upon the thief who steals an egg and cuts off his own hand."" And he steals the rope and cuts off his own hand.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
1056,"It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Do you recommend one of the limits set by Allah?” Then he stood up and delivered the sermon and said: “People! Verily, this is what killed the people before you: when an honorable man among them stole, they would let him go, and when a weak (low status) man stole, they would impose a limit on him.” (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are from Muslim)."
1057,Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “There is no punishment of dismemberment for the one who cheats and robs.”
1058,"It was narrated from Hazrat Rafi' bin Khadij (RA) that I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: ""There is no punishment for cutting off the hand while gleaning fruit and date-palm trees."""
1059,"It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Umayyah Makhzoomi (RA) that a thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). He confessed to the theft, but the goods were not found with him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to him: ""I do not think that you have stolen."" He said: Why not! (I stole.) You repeat the same two or three times. Then he gave the order and his hand was cut off. After that, he was brought to his service, and he said: ""Ask Allah's forgiveness for your sin and repent to Him."" He said: I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him, then he said three times: ""O Allah! Accept his repentance.'' In it is the saying of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace: ""Take him and cut off his hand, then mark him."""
1060,"On the authority of Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""When a limit is established on a thief, then no ransom (fine) will be imposed on him."""
1061,"Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, has narrated from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was asked about the dates hanging on the trees, and he said: ""There is no blame on a needy person if he eats them there and does not fill his feet."" And whoever leaves there with something, there is a ransom and a punishment. And whoever takes some of the dates after they reach the threshing floor and it is equal to the value of the shield, then the penalty of disobedience will be imposed on him."
1062,"It was narrated from Hazrat Safwan bin Umayyah that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: While he had ordered to cut off the hand of the man who had stolen his (Safwan's) cloak and he had interceded for him: ""Why did you not do this before bringing him to me (to forgive him?"")"
1063,"It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir (RA) that a thief was brought to the Prophet (PBUH) and he said: ""Kill him."" The people said: ""O Messenger of Allah! He has stolen."" He said: ""Cut off his hand."" So his hand was cut off. Then he was presented again, so he said: ""Kill him."" Hazrat Jabir (RA) mentioned it as before. Then it was brought for the third time, then mentioned in the same way. Then he was arrested and presented for the fourth time in the same way. Then he was arrested and presented for the fifth time, so he said: ""Kill him."""
1064,"It was narrated from Anas bin Malik (RA) that a man was brought to the Prophet (PBUH) who had drunk alcohol. You gave him about forty (40) lashes with two sticks. It is narrated by Anas (RA) that Hazrat Abu Bakr (RA) also gave this punishment. When Hazrat Umar (RA) came to the Caliphate, he consulted the Companions (RA). Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Auf (RA) said that the lightest punishment is eighty (80) lashes, so Hazrat Umar (RA) ordered the same. Every one of me is a saint and this is dearer to me. And in this hadith it is also said that a man testified against Waleed that he saw Waleed vomiting alcohol. On this Hazrat Uthman (RA) said: He had drunk and vomited."
1065,"Hazrat Mu'awiya (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said about a drunkard: ""When he drinks alcohol, flog him."" Then when he drinks alcohol again, whip him again. Then when he drinks the wine for the third time, then whip him again. Then when he drinks alcohol for the fourth time, blow his neck.”"
1066,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""When someone among you strikes, he should refrain from (striking) the face."" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
1067,"It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""There should be no boundaries in the mosques."" (Narrated by Tirmidhi and Al-Hakim)."
1068,"It is narrated from Hazrat Anas (RA) that when Allah revealed the sanctity of alcohol, only alcohol made from dates was drunk in Madinah at that time. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
1069,"It is narrated from Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the prohibition of alcohol was revealed, at that time it was prepared from five things: grapes, dates, honey, wheat and barley. And khamar (alcohol) is everything that covers the intellect. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
1070,Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Every intoxicating substance is wine and every intoxicating substance is forbidden.” (Muslim)
1071,"On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whatever is intoxicating in large quantities, even a small quantity of it is forbidden."""
1072,"It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that for the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) the Nabeez of Munqi was prepared in Mushkiza. You used to drink it on that day, on the second day and on the third day as well. Then, when it was the evening of the third day, he would drink it himself, make others drink, and if there was anything left, he would throw it away. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
1073,Hazrat Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Allah the Exalted has not placed healing for you in that which He has forbidden to you.” (Narrated by Bayhaqi and authenticated by Ibn Hibban).
1074,"It is narrated from Hazrat Wail Hazrami that Tariq bin Suwayd (RA) asked the Prophet (PBUH) about wine that he used to make it for medicine. He said: ""It is not a medicine but a disease."" (Narrated by Muslim, Abu Dawud and other imams)."
1075,"It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Barda Ansari that he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: ""No crime other than Allah's will should be punished with more than ten lashes."" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
1076,"Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Do not suffer from the mistakes of the Companions of the Most High, except that there are Shariah limits.”"
1077,"It is narrated from Hazrat Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: There is no such person that I would set a limit on him, and if he dies, I would feel sorry for him, except a drunkard. So if he dies, I will pay his dowry. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
1078,"It is narrated from Hazrat Saeed bin Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever is killed while protecting his property is a martyr."""
1079,It is narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Khabab that I heard my father narrating: He used to say that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: (After me) temptations will occur. O servant of Allah! So in these (times of temptations) do not become a victim and do not become a murderer.
